{- | DICT-SEMANTICS section 3: EMITTED LLVM IR. Replaces diff_compiler_dict_semantics_ir.sh.

   For each fixture entry in test/dict_fixtures, runs `medaka build --keep-ir`
   into a scratch dir and grades every table row against the kept `.ll`:
     HAS      -- at least one line matches the pattern
     LACKS    -- no line matches the pattern
     COUNT=n  -- exactly n lines match the pattern
   The table is the same 92 rows the shell gate carried, in the same order.
   Patterns are POSIX-ERE-equivalent; a pattern that does not compile is a
   failure, never a vacuous pass.

   PROVES: the emitted artifact's dictionary-parameter arity, dispatch routes
   and impl-symbol selection -- the properties behaviour alone cannot see
   (a dead dict slot, an arity skew, which impl a call site resolved to).
   DOES NOT PROVE: any runtime value, or behaviour under clang optimisation
   (the IR is produced before clang runs, so the patterns hold at -O0 and -O2).

   Floor: the table keeps at least 92 rows. A missing fixture file, a failed
   build, or a missing `.ll` is a failure. A drifted row is fixed by re-pinning
   that row here, with its rationale; see test/dict_fixtures/README.md.
   The grader itself (hitsOk) is self-checked by its own test block below.
-}

